@* Upstream's: the whole control disabled, showing its placeholder — and the same list with one
   option disabled inside it, because those are two different states and only one of them is
   about the control. A disabled option is still announced and still skipped, which is what tells
   a reader the choice exists and is not available to them. *@
<div class="flex w-full max-w-48 flex-col gap-4">
    <Select aria-label="Fruit" name="fruit" disabled>
        <SelectItem Value="" Selected>Select a fruit</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="apple">Apple</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="banana">Banana</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="blueberry">Blueberry</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="grapes">Grapes</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="pineapple">Pineapple</SelectItem>
    </Select>

    <Select aria-label="Fruit, one option unavailable" name="fruit-2">
        <SelectItem Value="" Selected>Select a fruit</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="apple">Apple</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="banana">Banana</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="blueberry">Blueberry</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="grapes" disabled>Grapes</SelectItem>
        <SelectItem Value="pineapple">Pineapple</SelectItem>
    </Select>
</div>
